  "lean": {
    "statement": ":\n    ∃ laws : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure ℝ,\n      (∀ n : ℕ, (laws n : Measure ℝ) =\n        (((Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ •\n          (Measure.count : Measure (Fin n → Bool))).map\n          (fun ε : Fin n → Bool => (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ *\n            ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1))) ∧\n      (laws 0 : Measure ℝ) = Measure.dirac 0 ∧\n      Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => laws (n + 1)) atTop\n        (𝓝 (⟨gaussianReal 0 1, inferInstance⟩ : ProbabilityMeasure ℝ))",
    "statement_sha256": "fea18bac8ce658a4bd35581a8fb112216e0fdfc56b8d2437313d3d9e92a8b91e",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Fin n is the finite type of indices smaller than n; Bool has two elements. All Fin n -> Bool configurations have their canonical finite measurable structure. The actual count/card law is counting measure scaled by the inverse actual carrier cardinal in ENNReal.",
      "The map is literal: true gives real1 and false gives real-1, summed over every coordinate, scaled by inverse Real.sqrt of n. The inverse is totalized with inverse0=0; the sum over Fin0 is empty.",
      "ProbabilityMeasure Real is the subtype of genuine real Borel probability measures equipped with its canonical weak measure topology. A witness in this subtype has total mass1. Measure.map is the actual measurable pushforward; Measure.dirac0 is the unit atom at real0.",
      "gaussianReal0 1 is the real Gaussian with mean0 and varianceNNReal1; it is a genuine probability measure. Tendsto with atTop and nhds on ProbabilityMeasure means weak-law convergence, and the displayed sequence uses n+1.",
      "The proposition is closed with no caller premises. The law family, all map equalities and the zero law and limit are outputs. No law, independence, moment, CLT, entropy, regularity or transport certificate is supplied."
    ]
  },
